eir own report.\n\n**What the goal requires:**\n- Only the Home tab is built at startup. The other tabs (Links, HeaderFooter, View, Review, Forms, Draw and the rest) are built the first time they are opened or requested.\n- LoadDoc must drop by more than the run spread.\n\n**Where it falls short:**\n\n1. **LoadDoc did not get faster.** Medians from the executor's 15 runs per side:\n\n   | Document | Before | After | Run spread |\n   |---|---:|---:|---:|\n   | large-100p | 1 264 ms | 1 191 ms | ≈300–600 ms |\n   | medium-10p | 1 222 ms | 1 224 ms | — |\n\n   - The large-100p drop of 73 ms is well inside the spread, and medium-10p shows no difference.\n   - The differential oracle's open timings agree: they vary by more than a second in both directions between cases.\n   - The rule for a performance goal is to reject when the measured difference against the original is absent or zero.\n\n2. **Most tabs are still built at startup.**\n   - Links, Review, Forms and Protect are untouched.\n   - Draw, Header & Footer and View are built on a 0 ms timer right after the document load call, so in practice still at startup.\n   - The executor says this is because some tabs put buttons into other tabs and expect their panel to exist when the app is ready. Making those tabs truly lazy needs changes outside this packet's file list.\n\n3. **The executor's own profile points to a different cause.** Most of the Toolbar's ≈200–250 ms before LoadDoc comes from the toolbar view drawing its own panels (Insert, Layout, References), not from these tab controllers. The executor recorded a follow-up request for that in `.theseus/spawn/`.\n\n**Other points to fix:**\n- **An ordering risk remains open.** If the app ever finished loading before the 0 ms timer fired, the late-built tabs would miss their setup step. The executor notes this in the log but never observed it.\n- **The browser check that the late-built tabs come out the same was never committed.** The differential only compares the visible Home tab, and no unit test was added under `tests/unit`.\n\nThe follow-up in `.theseus/spawn/` is the better route. Either retarget this packet (with the extra files it needs) or close it in favour of the follow-up. A redo should commit the tab-equivalence check under `.theseus/oracle/perf` and keep the reversed-order measuring method.\n\nVERDICT: REJECT LoadDoc does not drop by more than the run spread (1264→1191 ms against a ≈300–600 ms spread, medium-10p unchanged) and the hidden tabs are still built at startup; the real cost is in view/Toolbar.js panel drawing, so retarget or rely on the spawned follow-up","ttft_ms":3659,"type":"result","duration_ms":18768,"uuid":"fdd94477-bce1-4e3b-823d-38759ef39fec","ttft_stream_ms":2623,"time_to_request_ms":233,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":4,"system_prompt":156,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":3,"input_attachments":13,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":4,"tool_pool_refresh":1,"init_message":4,"init_frame_send":2,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":2,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":0,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":8,"query_setup":2,"auto_mode_context_wait":5,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":13,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":1,"request_build":6},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":28,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":117,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":210,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":139,"process_rss_mib_result":216,"process_anon_mib_result":131,"process_peak_rss_mib":243,"process_cpu_ms_turn":944,"process_wall_ms_turn":18768,"process_cpu_ms_streaming":183,"process_wall_ms_streaming":5293,"main_stream_count":4,"main_stream_event_count":219,"main_stream_chunk_count":67,"process_turn_states":{"main_stream":{"cpu_ms":183,"wall_ms":5293,"entries":4},"tool":{"cpu_ms":35,"wall_ms":77,"entries":2},"first_event_wait":{"cpu_ms":512,"wall_ms":13073,"entries":4},"before_first_request":{"cpu_ms":116